...|.|.|.|.|.|X|X|O|O|X|O|..."  \nColumns: A to O  \nSo:  \nF9: X, G9: X, H9: O, I9: O, J9: X, K9: O\n\nAh! **I9 is O (White)**, not X!  \nMy mistake.\n\nCorrecting:  \n- I5: X  \n- I6: X  \n- I7: X  \n- I8: X  \n- I9: O ← So only four Xs from I5 to I8, but I9 is O — so not five.\n\nSimilarly, **H5: X, H6: X, H7: X, H8: X, H9: O** — again, broken.\n\nNow check **G5: X, G6: X, G7: X, G8: X, G9: X** — is this possible?\n\nRow 5: G5: X ✅  \nRow 6: G6: O ❌\n\nNo — G6 is O. So not possible.\n\nWait — actually, from the board:\n- Row 6: C6(O), then G6: O? Wait no:\n\nBoard row 6: "|.|.|O|.|.|.|O|X|X|X|.|.|.|.|.|.|"\n\nSo:\n- C6: O\n- G6: O? Column G is 7th letter → A(1), B(2), C(3), D(4), E(5), F(6), G(7)\n\nSo row 6: after F6 (empty), G6: O? The entry says: "|.|.|O|.|.|.|O|X|X|X|." → positions:\nA6: ., B6: ., C6: O, D6: ., E6: ., F6: ., G6: O, H6: X, I6: X, J6: X, K6: .\n\nSo **G6: O**, yes.\n\nSo G5: X, G6: O — broken.\n\nNow consider **diagonal from E7 to J12**:  \nE7: X, F7: X, G7: X, H7: X, I7: X → that’s **E7, F7, G7, H7, I7** — all X?\n\nCheck:\n- E7: X ✅ (from row 7: D7(X), E7(O)? Wait!)\n\nRow 7: "|.|.|.|X|O|X|X|X|X|O|."\n\nBreakdown:\n- D7: X\n- E7: O\n- F7: X\n- G7: X\n- H7: X\n- I7: X\n- J7: O\n\nSo E7 is O — so F7 to I7: F7(X), G7(X), H7(X), I7(X) — that’s **four in a row horizontally on row 7**, from F7 to I7.\n\nBut F7 to I7 is columns F,G,H,I — four stones: F7, G7, H7, I7 — all X.\n\nJ7 is O, E7 is O — so blocked on both sides.\n\nNow vertical in **column G**:  \nG5: X  \nG6: O  \nG7: X  \nG8: X  \nG9: X  \nG10: X? G10 is listed — from row 10: E10: O, F10: O, G10: X → yes.\n\nSo:\n- G5: X\n- G6: O → breaks\nNot useful.\n\nNow look at **column J**:\nJ5: O\nJ6: X\nJ7: O\nJ8: X\nJ9: X\nSo mixed.\n\nNow consider **diagonals**.\n\nTry **backward diagonal (top-left to bottom-right)** passing through center.\n\nLook at **F7: X, G8: X, H9: O** — broken.\n\nWhat about **D7: X, E6: ?**\n\nE6: from row 6: E6 is empty.\n\nTry **G5: X, H6: X, I7: X, J8: X, K9: O** — K9 is O, so J8 is X, but K9 would be next — not helpful.\n\nWait — **H5: X, I6: X, J7: O** — broken.\n\nNow try **forward diagonal (top-right to bottom-left)**.\n\nFor example: **I5: X, H6: X, G7: X, F8: O** — F8 is O, so G7 to I5 is three: I5, H6, G7 — all X.\n\nCan we extend?\n\nAfter G7, next would be F8: O — blocked.\n\nAnother: **J6: X, I7: X, H8: X, G9: X** — J6, I7, H8, G9 — that’s four in a diagonal going down-left.\n\nCheck:\n- J6: X ✅\n- I7: X ✅\n- H8: X ✅\n- G9: X ✅\n- Next: F10: O ✅ (from row 10: F10: O)\n\nSo F10 is O — blocks continuation.\n\nBut what about extending upward? After J6, is there K5? K5: O — not X.\n\nSo only four: J6, I7, H8, G9 — diagonal from J6 to G9.\n\nAll X, and F10 is O — blocked.\n\nBut wait — is there a **five-in-a-row already formed**?\n\nLet’s check **row 7**: D7: X, E7: O, F7: X, G7: X, H7: X, I7: X, J7: O — so F7 to I7: four Xs.\n\nNo five.\n\nNow check **column H**:\nH5: X\nH6: X\nH7: X\nH8: X\nH9: O — only four.\n\nColumn I: I5: X, I6: X, I7: X, I8: X, I9: O — four.\n\nColumn G: G5: X, G6: O — broken.\n\nWait — **row 9**: F9: X, G9: X, H9: O, I9: O, J9: X — not helpful.\n\nNow, is there any move that creates **five in a row**?\n\nLet’s look for **open 4s** or **winning moves**.\n\nConsider **extending the diagonal G9-H8-I7-J6** — it’s currently G9, H8, I7, J6 — all X, going up-right.\n\nTo complete five, we need **K5** — is K5 available?\n\nK5: from row 5: K5: O → occupied by White.\n\nSo cannot play K5.\n\nDown-left extension: after G9, next is F10: O — blocked.\n\nSo cannot extend.\n\nNow, what about **creating a 5-in-a-row horizontally on row 8**?\n\nRow 8: ..., F8: O, G8: X, H8: X, I8: X, J8: X, K8: O\n\nSo G8 to J8: four Xs — if we could play at **F8 or K8**, but both are occupied.\n\nNo space.\n\nSame on row 7: F7 to I7: four Xs, but E7 and J7 are O — no room.\n\nNow vertical: column H: H5 to H8: four Xs (H5, H6, H7, H8), H9: O — so cannot extend down. Up: H4: O — also blocked.\n\nSimilarly column I: I5 to I8: four Xs,