nd E5 is within bounds.\n\nSo playing **E5** completes a horizontal line: E5, F5, G5, H5, I5 — all X.\n\nThat’s five in a row.\n\nIs this valid?\n\nConfirm coordinates:\n- Column E = 5th column\n- Row 5\n- Board[5][E] = currently empty\n- After placing X at E5, we have: E5, F5, G5, H5, I5 — all X → 5 in a row.\n\nYes! This is a **winning move**.\n\nNo other move needed — this wins the game.\n\nReason:  \nPlaying at E5 completes a horizontal five-in-a-row from E5 to I5, which is unbroken and not blocked (since J5 is O but we don’t need it — E5 to I5 is exactly five). This move wins the game immediately.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "E", "row": 5}'}
